{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Big Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Getting Over It", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use these tenses  to express that an action began in the past and is still going on or has just finished. The past action is <span class=\"strong\">connected to the present</span> in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To talk about a <span class=\"strong\">result</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">recently completed action</span>, use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect tense</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Regular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Irregular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + past participle of irregular verbs", "type": "text"}, {"content": " To talk about the duration of an action, use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Continuous</span> is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + <span class=\"italic\">been</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: It feels like <span class=\"strong\">you've been thinking</span> a lot about Camilla lately.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Of course I have! In fact, <span class=\"strong\">I've been trying</span> to get in touch with her recently. <span class=\"strong\">I've been</span> so unlucky with my dates lately. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Showing You Understand Someone's Feelings or Situation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Showing <span class=\"strong\">empathy</span> is an important part of natural conversation. It means that you understand someone else's situation. It makes the other person more comfortable talking to you, which can extend the conversation. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to show <span class=\"strong\">empathy</span>, use expressions like: <br> <span class=\"italic\">It sounds like ... </span><br> <span class=\"italic\">It feels like ... <br/> <br/></span> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">It sounds like the two of you were confused.<br/>It feels like you've been thinking a lot about this.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It feels like you could learn a lot from him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It sounds like you've been having a hard time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It feels like you have more to say about the subject.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It seems like I could do more to help you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have a crush", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be infatuated with someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally told me that Camilla has a crush on me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about an emotional situation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "obvious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "predictable and easily understood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I only 